      "summary": "Backstrap loom; made of wood; with a section of weft-brocaded textile in burgundy, yellow and green wool on white cotton ground already woven. Basic construction: 1) twined rope to wrap around tree; 2) dowel at top, wrapped with green &quot;heading cords&quot;; 3) dowel twined through weft threads; 4) dowel twined through weft threads; 5) flat piece of wood with tapered ends; 6) thin flat piece of wood with tapered ends; 7) dowel with &quot;heading cord&quot; wrapped around it; 8) weaver&#039;s strap (mecapal in Spanish) plaited from vegetable fibre for strapping around weaver&#039;s waist.",
